{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1230 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "15e036f6e2dd11f3ca607cf2a6b9ef78f337f71830d761c5bc7ba13aeba376ad" :edb/db-before-t 1229 :edb/db-after-t 1230 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534542 50 #inst "2026-10-12T02:27:33.289Z" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186096834 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424993 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186096836 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424992 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186096910 1050 1320.0 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186097927 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.\n$$\n\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n\n$$\n\\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe usually let $u = x,$ but that would leave us with $v' = \\ln(x)$ which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our $u$ and $v'$ slightly differently, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{'}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{'}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\operatorname{ln}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {{\\operatorname{ln}x}_{⏟}}_{u}\\cdot {{x}_{⏟}}_{{v}^{'}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should *always* identify the logarithmic function with $u,$ not with $v'.$" 13194139534542 17592186045417 false] [17592186097927 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.\n$$\n\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n\n$$\n\\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe usually let $u = x,$ but that would leave us with $v' = \\ln(x)$ which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our $u$ and $v'$ slightly differently, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{u}\\cdot {{x}_{⏟}}_{{v}^{′}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should *always* identify the logarithmic function with $u,$ not with $v'.$" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186320707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424989 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186320707 1078 #edb/ref 17592186319492 13194139534542 17592186045417 false] [17592186320707 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424989 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424983 1080 "\\frac{4e^5+1}{25}" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424983 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424983 1083 #uuid "1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424984 1080 "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424984 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424984 1083 #uuid "1fac7b1b-401e-571f-9ac1-c8035cba4079" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424985 1080 "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424985 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424985 1083 #uuid "612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424986 1080 "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424986 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424986 1083 #uuid "92b952c7-daa6-5ab4-a7f5-81b3cf909d3a" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424987 1080 "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424987 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424987 1083 #uuid "bd63e3cd-ff82-5ade-9211-594e2bfdb08c" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424988 1080 "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424988 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424988 1083 #uuid "cc74e90b-cf7b-5156-89e6-293ad43d67ea" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424989 1080 "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424989 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424989 1083 #uuid "e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424984 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424985 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424986 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424987 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424988 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1077 "selection" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424985 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424990 1079 #uuid "8afc707b-a42b-5621-ace9-e6a014a201bb" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424991 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424983 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424991 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424991 1077 "field-1" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424991 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424983 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424991 1079 #uuid "9e0c4dfe-2a2c-535e-956d-62ad8cee8229" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424992 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424990 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424992 1069 "q-78972" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424992 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424992 1071 "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424992 1072 #uuid "45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424992 1074 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424993 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424991 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424993 1069 "q-350842" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424993 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424993 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424993 1072 #uuid "48a4330e-b61a-5908-b482-77c947469ce8" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true] [17592186424993 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\,dx=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{1}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{5}]-\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}}{5}-(\\frac{{e}^{5}}{25}-\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(5{e}^{5}-{e}^{5}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(4{e}^{5}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534542 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" 17592186424983 "answer-1fac7b1b-401e-571f-9ac1-c8035cba4079" 17592186424984 "answer-612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" 17592186424985 "answer-92b952c7-daa6-5ab4-a7f5-81b3cf909d3a" 17592186424986 "answer-bd63e3cd-ff82-5ade-9211-594e2bfdb08c" 17592186424987 "answer-cc74e90b-cf7b-5156-89e6-293ad43d67ea" 17592186424988 "answer-e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" 17592186424989 "answer-field-8afc707b-a42b-5621-ace9-e6a014a201bb" 17592186424990 "answer-field-9e0c4dfe-2a2c-535e-956d-62ad8cee8229" 17592186424991 "question-45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54" 175921864249